cff-version: 1.2.0
title: HyperStrata
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
message: >-
  Personal experiments, live in public repo. Not competing, just learning
  for fun on my rig. Tuned for one rig only: RTX 3070 Ti Laptop 8GB plus
  32GB RAM. Runs on other RTX cards in theory, no proof, no promise.
  Upstream never approved, supported, or endorsed this fork. If you use
  it, cite it as below.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/theacidblack/HyperStrata
authors:
  - given-names: Acid
    family-names: Black
    alias: theacidblack
    email: itsmyacidblack@gmail.com
    website: https://github.com/theacidblack
abstract: >-
  HyperStrata is a personal learning fork for running 35-billion-parameter
  models on 8 GB VRAM plus 32 GB RAM on Windows with NVIDIA CUDA. It forks
  PolyStrata 0.1.44.1 at commit 51dc2427 (https://github.com/VecSzn/PolyStrata),
  which builds on Strata (https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata). Chain is
  Strata to PolyStrata to HyperStrata. Version 1.0.0 is the first public
  run, 2026-10-17. No wide support, no maintenance promise.
keywords:
  - local-llm-inference
  - qwen3
  - mixture-of-experts
  - GGUF
  - KV-cache
  - quantization
  - CUDA
  - Windows
  - 8GB-VRAM
